nodes.text:
Create five one-hour reading group calendar events with Google Calendar, one per day Monday 2026-03-16 through Friday 2026-03-20, always 10:00–11:00 UTC. Use UTC wall-clock times with the "Z" suffix (no timeZone field needed) so the schedule is unambiguous.

Create these exact events via mcp__google_calendar__create_event:

1. summary: "Reading Group: Chain-of-Thought"
   start: {"dateTime": "2026-03-16T10:00:00Z"}
   end: {"dateTime": "2026-03-16T11:00:00Z"}
   description: "Paper: Chain-of-Thought Prompting Elicits Reasoning in Large Language Models (Jason Wei, Xuezhi Wang, Dale Schuurmans et al., arXiv:2201.11903, 2022). Focus: few-shot prompting with intermediate reasoning steps."

2. summary: "Reading Group: Tree-of-Thought"
   start: {"dateTime": "2026-03-17T10:00:00Z"}
   end: {"dateTime": "2026-03-17T11:00:00Z"}
   description: "Paper: Tree of Thoughts: Deliberate Problem Solving with Large Language Models (Shunyu Yao, Dian Yu, Jeffrey Zhao et al., arXiv:2305.10601, 2023). Focus: tree-structured search over thoughts with self-evaluation and backtracking."

3. summary: "Reading Group: Self-Consistency"
   start: {"dateTime": "2026-03-18T10:00:00Z"}
   end: {"dateTime": "2026-03-18T11:00:00Z"}
   description: "Paper: Self-Consistency Improves Chain of Thought Reasoning in Language Models (Xuezhi Wang, Jason Wei, Dale Schuurmans et al., arXiv:2203.11171, 2022). Focus: diverse path sampling with majority-vote decoding."

4. summary: "Reading Group: Step-by-Step Verification"
   start: {"dateTime": "2026-03-19T10:00:00Z"}
   end: {"dateTime": "2026-03-19T11:00:00Z"}
   description: "Paper: Let's Verify Step by Step (Hunter Lightman, Vineet Kosaraju, Yura Burda et al., arXiv:2305.20050, 2023). Focus: process supervision and process reward models for verifying reasoning steps."

5. summary: "Reading Group: Automatic Chain-of-Thought"
   start: {"dateTime": "2026-03-20T10:00:00Z"}
   end: {"dateTime": "2026-03-20T11:00:00Z"}
   description: "Paper: Automatic Chain of Thought Prompting in Large Language Models (Zhuosheng Zhang, Aston Zhang, Mu Li et al., arXiv:2210.03629, 2022). Focus: Auto-CoT demonstration construction via clustering and zero-shot chain generation."

After creating all five, VERIFY with mcp__google_calendar__list_events using timeMin "2026-03-16T00:00:00Z" and timeMax "2026-03-21T00:00:00Z", and confirm each of the five events appears with the correct 10:00–11:00 UTC times. If any event failed to create, retry it before finishing.

REPORT BACK: the 5 event IDs, their summaries, their exact start/end times as returned by the calendar, and the verification listing.
Schedule 5 reading group events
